# AAASM-5809 dogfood driver — the confined arm's baseline policy.
#
# Rendered by `../../policy/render.sh` (reused, not copied) into a concrete
# policy before a run — the write grant below needs the scratch directory's
# actual path, which is only known once the driver picks one.
#
# What this states, and why:
#
# - `filesystem.read.allow: ["/"]` — the driver invokes real developer
#   tooling (a C compiler, python3, git) whose binaries and libraries live
#   wherever the runner image put them; read confinement is not what this
#   policy exercises (the sandlock/aasm-native suites already cover that in
#   AAASM-5708/5802).
# - `filesystem.write.allow` — only the scratch tree's `permitted/` subtree.
#   `permitted/` and `forbidden/` are siblings under the same scratch root so
#   a scenario that expects a write to land can be told apart from one that
#   expects it denied by which subtree it targets, not by a different policy
#   file.
# - `capabilities: allow: [terminal_exec, file_read, file_write,
#   file_delete]` — this is the "spawn works" arm: the driver's spawn-child,
#   descendant-confinement and compiler/package tooling scenarios all need
#   `aasm run` to permit the confined process to fork further children.
#   `confined-no-exec.yaml.tmpl` is this file's opposite, used for the
#   "capability denied" scenario.
#
#   `capabilities.allow` is a genuine allow-list, not a per-capability toggle
#   (`aa-isolation/src/lowering.rs`'s `restriction_sources` — a capability
#   omitted from an in-force allow-list is restricted, matching
#   `aa_gateway::PolicyEngine::capability_guard`'s L7 reading of the same
#   node). Naming only `terminal_exec` here silently swept `file_read`/
#   `file_write`/`file_delete` into whole-domain prevention regardless of
#   what `filesystem.read.allow`/`filesystem.write.allow` below separately
#   state — the two nodes intersect, they don't compose independently.
#   `file_write` and `file_delete` are two distinct `Capability` variants
#   that both lower to the one `filesystem_write` domain
#   (`aa-isolation/src/lowering.rs`'s `write()` call passes
#   `&[Capability::FileWrite, Capability::FileDelete]`) — naming only
#   `file_write` still left `file_delete` "omitted" and the whole write
#   domain fell back to prevention despite `file_write` itself being
#   granted; both must be named for the domain to narrow.
apiVersion: agent-assembly/v1
kind: Policy
metadata:
  name: aaasm-5809-dogfood-confined
spec:
  tools:
    "*":
      allow: true
  filesystem:
    read:
      allow:
        - "/"
    write:
      allow:
        - "__SCRATCH_ROOT__/permitted"
        - "/dev/null"
  capabilities:
    allow:
      - terminal_exec
      - file_read
      - file_write
      - file_delete
  network:
    allowlist:
      - "127.0.0.1"
